	(text "DESIGN VALUES (LMQ66430-Q1 SNVSBV1F; TPS3702-Q1 SBVS261C; Node60 DEC-004, DEC-006). Values per D-45.\nPower-up order (DEC-004): VDDAU_AON always on -> LAN8670 INH high -> U302 3V3_MAIN -> 3V3_MAIN > 2.46 V\n  -> U303 1V5_CORE. VDDA <= VDDAU + 0.5 V holds because VDDAU is up first. No FS26, latch or MCU gate.\n0R debug links (project default: every regulator output): R on each *_REG -> rail, 0603 rated 2 A.\n  Feedback senses the regulator side, so opening the link leaves the regulator in regulation.\nU302 3V3_MAIN: LMQ66430MC3 fixed 3.3 V (VOUT/FB on the output), 2.2 MHz, MODE/SYNC = GND (auto PFM/PWM).\n  TI Table 8-4: L 2.2uH, COUT >= 40 uF effective -> 2 x 22uF 10V 1210 + 100nF; CIN 2 x 4.7uF 100V + 100nF 100V\n  (100 V = >= 2x the 34 V OV cut-off). CVCC 1uF. BOOT: internal 0.1 uF (TI: CBOOT DNP), so no-connect. PG unused.\nU303 1V5_CORE: adjustable. VOUT = 1 V x (1 + 14k / 28k) = 1.50 V. RFBT || RFBB = 9.33 k: inside the 5-10 k\n  window that selects adjustable mode (Eq. 4); RFBT <= 15 k (Eq. 5).\n  L = (VIN - VOUT) / (fSW x K x 3 A) x VOUT / VIN = 0.99 uH (12 V in, K = 0.2) -> 1uH. COUT 3 x 22uF.\n  At 12 V in the on-time is 57 ns, below tON-MIN (65-75 ns): the part stretches off-time at high VIN.\n  Check ripple and EMI from 14 to 34 V on the bench.\nEN chain: 3V3_MAIN - 100k - 1V5_EN - 100k - GND. EN rises at 1.23 V (1.16-1.30 V): 1V5 starts at\n  3V3_MAIN > 2.32-2.60 V and stops below 1.66-2.00 V.\nWake timing (GATE-NET-01, accepted 2026-10-23, to be measured): OPEN Alliance limit is supply ramp + PHY init\n  <= 15 ms (Sleep/Wake-Up Electrical Interface Spec v1.0 sec. 5.2); the LAN8670 \"1 ms\" is Microchip's allocation.\n  3V3_MAIN ~2.5 ms EN delay + 2-4.6 ms soft start, LAN8670 D0 ~2 ms POR + 0.9 ms init: ~10 ms expected.\nU304 TPS3702AX33, SET = GND: UV 3.10 V / OV 3.50 V (+/-6 % window, 0.55 % hysteresis, +/-0.9 %).\n  The SET-high +/-2 % window (3.23 / 3.37 V) is too tight for buck transients. UV and OV open drains are\n  wired-OR onto RESET_L with 4.7k to 3V3_MAIN. No internal reset delay: release timing comes from\n  the S32K344 reset sequence (GATE-SUP-02).\nU301 TPS7B8133QWDRVRQ1: 40 V, Iq 3.5 uA (above the 1-2 uA Rev A target). EN tied to IN (always on); DNC open;\n  thermal pad to GND. COUT 2.2uF 10V 0603 (datasheet: 1-200 uF effective, ESR 1 mOhm-5 Ohm), CIN 1uF 100V.\nInductors (user choice 2026-10-23): Wurth 74438356022HT 2.2 uH (Isat 7.6 A) and 74438356010HT 1.0 uH (Isat 9.3 A),\n  -55..+150 C. Check the 2.2 MHz core loss in Wurth REDEXPERT before release.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
